{
  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: Multiprofile aggregation (avgpool) produced the largest single gain observed (~13 points, 52%→65%), making aggregation the highest-leverage design axis. The scvi_n200 encoder added a modest +3.5 points over PCA, and image-only signal is very weak (~21%). Uncertainty: We do not yet know whether the aggregation *strategy* (avgpool vs. transformer) matters, or whether ~65% is near the RNA-only ceiling. This experiment (config_006) directly tests transformer aggregation in an otherwise identical setup to config_005 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200), isolating the aggregation architecture as the sole variable. If transformer substantially improves over avgpool, it signals that richer aggregation will be critical in multimodal fusion and justifies prioritizing transformer-based configs later. If it does not, it confirms avgpool is near-optimal, simplifying the search space and letting us focus budget on encoder choice or fusion strategy. This is the best use of the next experiment because it exploits the strongest evidence (multiprofile is the key lever) while reducing uncertainty on a sub-decision that will gate many future multimodal configurations, all without introducing the additional confounds of a new modality or encoder."
}

